# LEX I — systemd stays at 259.
# 259 predates the userdb birthDate field. Ubuntu 26.04 ships 259 for its whole
# life; this law stops a PPA or backport from bringing in 260 or later.
# (APT version pins take * and ? but not [ranges], hence one block per prefix.)
Explanation: Lex I: hold systemd at 259
